('advanced-native-826', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-826-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["It is an essential condition for sharing ideas openly."],"options":["It is important only for the final public presentation.","It is an essential condition for sharing ideas openly.","It concerns how the final result looks, rather than whether members can question unfinished ideas.","It means every idea is accepted without discussion."]},"advanced-native-826-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Members need to feel able to share ideas before they are fully formed.","It is at the heart of teamwork because people need to share unfinished ideas without fear of ridicule.","People contribute more openly when they do not expect ridicule.","Our discussions depend on being able to question and explain without personal attacks."],"options":["Members need to feel able to share ideas before they are fully formed.","It is at the heart of teamwork because people need to share unfinished ideas without fear of ridicule.","People contribute more openly when they do not expect ridicule.","Our discussions depend on being able to question and explain without personal attacks."]},"advanced-native-826-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Understanding is at the heart of the group’s choices."],"options":["Understanding is considered only after every activity has been chosen.","Understanding is at the heart of the group’s choices.","The group chooses mainly by how colourful the activities look."]},"advanced-native-826-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["No other relevant factor can have any importance."],"options":["No other relevant factor can have any importance.","The reason for that central role should be clear from context.","A factor is central to the issue being discussed."]},"advanced-native-826-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Trust is at the heart of teamwork, but clear roles still help us put that trust into practice."],"options":["Trust is at the heart of teamwork, but clear